      "B": {
        "reading_checked": "If low usage requires standard follow-up unless a stated critical threshold or escalation rule is met, then a visibly low May value alone supports standard low-usage follow-up rather than critical escalation. The chart supplies no printed critical threshold, baseline, or routing rule; this interpretation assumes escalation cannot be inferred solely from relative bar height.",
        "evidence": "The necessary condition is the absence of a stated critical threshold or escalation rule. A review of the chart confirms no such rule is printed. The task instructions also do not provide a numeric cutoff or policy table defining 'critical' vs 'standard'. Therefore, the condition that no explicit rule exists is met. The interpretation that a low value alone supports standard follow-up is a valid reading of the available evidence, as there is no basis to infer a critical status from the visual data alone.",
